From 17b267ea59d52bf430f5ec2273adbb490ce84945 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 02:06:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] drm/msm: fix NULL deref when SUBMIT is a context's first
 VM user

msm_ioctl_gem_submit() reads to_msm_vm(ctx->vm)->unusable before anything
has created the context's VM.  ctx->vm is allocated lazily by
msm_context_vm(), which every other user goes through -- including
submit_create() a little further down the same ioctl.  A GEM_SUBMIT
issued before any ioctl that touches the VM therefore dereferences NULL.

Mesa never hits this because it allocates buffers and asks for their
iovas first, but it is reachable by any unprivileged process with a
render node open, which makes it a local denial of service:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000003c5
  CPU: 3 UID: 10000 PID: 1929 Comm: msmsubmit
  pc : msm_ioctl_gem_submit+0x60/0x1834
  Call trace:
   msm_ioctl_gem_submit+0x60/0x1834 (P)
   drm_ioctl_kernel+0xc0/0x134
   drm_ioctl+0x1fc/0x4c0
   __arm64_sys_ioctl+0xa4/0x100

Found while writing a bring-up prober that submitted before allocating.
Route the check through msm_context_vm() like every other caller.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
index 3c6bc90c3..6c62b993d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_submit.c
@@ -572,7 +572,7 @@ int msm_ioctl_gem_submit(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
 	if (args->pad)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (to_msm_vm(ctx->vm)->unusable)
+	if (to_msm_vm(msm_context_vm(dev, ctx))->unusable)
 		return UERR(EPIPE, dev, "context is unusable");
 
 	/* for now, we just have 3d pipe.. eventually this would need to
